# GitHub language detection
#
# This repository holds seven client SDKs. Without these rules GitHub measures
# every tracked file, so the reference applications and the most verbose test
# suite decide the repository's language label rather than the libraries people
# actually install. The rules below take the demos, the test suites and the
# generated files out of the count, leaving the seven shipped libraries.
#
# GitHub still names whichever library is largest as the primary language; what
# changes is that the breakdown reflects the SDKs instead of the demos.

# Reference applications — demonstrations, not part of any published package.
sdks/*/minimal-app/**           linguist-vendored
sdks/dotnet/samples/**          linguist-vendored

# Test suites.
sdks/node/src/__tests__/**      linguist-vendored
sdks/python/tests/**            linguist-vendored
sdks/php/tests/**               linguist-vendored
sdks/dotnet/tests/**            linguist-vendored
sdks/java/connect-sdk/src/test/** linguist-vendored
sdks/ruby/spec/**               linguist-vendored
sdks/go/**/*_test.go            linguist-vendored
sdks/go/testsupport/**          linguist-vendored

# Generated and lock files.
**/package-lock.json            linguist-generated
**/composer.lock                linguist-generated
**/Gemfile.lock                 linguist-generated
**/go.sum                       linguist-generated

# Documentation should not count towards the language breakdown.
*.md                            linguist-documentation
